          "at0079.1" : {
            "@type" : "ARCHETYPE_TERM",
            "code" : "at0079.1",
            "text" : "Completeness of sample",
            "description" : "Narrative description about the collection of the specimen."
          },
          "at0067.1" : {
            "@type" : "ARCHETYPE_TERM",
            "code" : "at0067.1",
            "text" : "Location of sample production",
            "description" : "Identification of the physical setting in which the specimen is collected.",
            "comment" : "For example: laboratory outpatient clinic, at home, or hospital ward. This specifies the type of specimen collection location within the healthcare environment. The specimen collection setting may provide additional information relevant to the analysis of the result."
          },
          "at0008.1" : {
            "@type" : "ARCHETYPE_TERM",
            "code" : "at0008.1",
            "text" : "Date of last ejaculation",
            "description" : "The context in which the specimen is collected.",
            "comment" : "For example: 'fasting'; 'full bladder'; 'sterile field'; or special instructions on the handling or immediate processing of the sample, such as 'centrifuge on receipt'. This data element also be used to document any known deviations from collection or handling instructions, for example that the patient had not fasted, even when this had been originally requested. Coding of the 'Sampling context' with a terminology is preferred, where possible.\r\n\r\nIf this archetype is used within an INSTRUCTION archetype, the context will reflect the intended or desired conditions at sample collection. If this archetype is used for representing an ACTION archetype pathway step which correlates with the collection being performed or completed, the context will be reflecting the conditions that existed at sample collection and this may also be copied to the 'Confounding factors' element of the OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result archetype."
          }
        },
